<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shemamun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1280s–1290s</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Semamun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shemamun was a king of Makuria in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> in the late 13th century, repeatedly deposed and restored. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> armies sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qalawun">Qalawun</a> in the late 1280s installed rival princes at Dongola, but Shemamun regained the throne each time the Egyptian troops withdrew. His struggles show how far Mamluk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> controlled Makurian successions after 1276.</p></div>
